&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Garda Capital Partners (Garda) is a multi-billion dollar alternative investment firm with over 22 years of experience deploying relative value strategies across fixed income markets for institutional investors. We hire, grow, and mentor great talent and remain steadfast in our commitment to building a culture that helps them succeed. Garda is more than a workplace. We are built on trust, integrity, and a shared vision for how we work together, the enduring relationships we build, and the consistency of our results. Garda&#39;s primary offices are located in Wayzata, New York City, West Palm Beach, Geneva, Zug, Copenhagen, Singapore, and Scottsdale.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Garda is seeking an Infrastructure Engineer to own Platform Engineering &amp;amp; Automation. This hands-on role builds and operates shared deployment capabilities for infrastructure and selected applications, while providing advanced infrastructure engineering and production support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The engineer develops reusable deployment pipelines, infrastructure templates, and self-service workflows that help teams provision environments and release changes consistently — working with architecture, application owners, and regional teams to improve platform reliability and resolve complex infrastructure problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Escalation &amp;amp; Infrastructure Support&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a senior escalation point for complex infrastructure incidents and recurring operational problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot across Windows/Linux systems, identity, networking, cloud, virtualization, storage, and backup&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead root-cause analysis and convert recurring incidents into engineering work or documented standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in major changes, recovery events, and follow-the-sun handoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Platform Engineering &amp;amp; Deployment Automation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build automation using PowerShell, Python, and APIs with production-quality testing and error handling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own reusable infrastructure-as-code and configuration templates (Terraform, Ansible)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and operate CI/CD pipelines for infrastructure and applications, including validation, environment promotion, health checks, and rollback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply Git, peer review, automated tests, change controls, and secure secrets handling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Observability, Reliability &amp;amp; Standards&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve monitoring, logging, metrics, dashboards, alerting, and automated health checks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tune operational signals to reduce noise and improve detection/recovery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain reusable provisioning workflows and self-service capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own platform reliability and lifecycle improvements with service owners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technical Leadership&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers and workplace technology staff in troubleshooting and automation practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review infrastructure code and pipeline designs with architecture, Security, and application owners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain runbooks, diagrams, and onboarding guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a prioritized platform backlog with the architect and regional leads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Desired Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4–6 years of hands-on infrastructure operations experience across several domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in IT, computer science, computer engineering, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced PowerShell or Python automation experience, including API integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with infrastructure as code or configuration management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and supporting CI/CD pipelines (Git, testing, secure deployment, rollback)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting, root-cause analysis, and incident-response skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of monitoring, logging, alerting, and observability concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to document work, mentor others, and collaborate across a distributed team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Preference for experience with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS, container platforms, modern cloud operating patterns (Azure a plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering reusable provisioning workflows for infrastructure and business applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ITSM, change, incident, and problem-management practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in financial services or another performance-sensitive environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of solving complex infrastructure problems and building shared capabilities other teams can use independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of maintaining high standards for reliability, documentation, and maintainability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience remaining effective under pressure, with a history of mentoring and knowledge-sharing within teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gardacp.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Candidate_Privacy_Notice.pdf&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Snr Director West International Cluster, &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Rare BU - Closing Date: November 13, 2027.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be responsible to develop and execute all sales and marketing activities in the relative cluster of countries, with immediate focus on driving the development of GIVLAARI and OXLUMO.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This person will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and challenge regional and local teams in tailoring the global strategy to the specific markets while maintaining global/regional alignment;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Allocate investment and drive and track focused execution of cross-functional tactics;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share learnings and best practices across the Global Rare Business Unit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will lead a team of &amp;nbsp;Field Business Leaders (FBL) across a group of geographies and be the primary interface with local Country Managers and International TTR BU shared services (eg Regional Commercial, Business Operations and and Market Access). They will appropriately partner with Medical and Regional Marketing to ensure optimal alignment, insight sharing and communication. &amp;nbsp;The Cluster Head will also build and execute the Cluster tactical plan (e.g.,Sales force and HCP target group prioritization,&amp;nbsp; congress activities, marketing materials) and participate in the regional tactics as appropriate (e.g., European congresses).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Cluster Head reports to the VP, International Rare Head.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manages the full Commercial Team for the specific geographies (Field Business Leaders and their KAMs)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maximize the commercial potential of Alnylam’s assets through the development and implementation of strategic/operational plans in close collaboration with Global Rare marketing, Medical Affairs and Market Access teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, plan and set the commercial direction for the business within the Cluster, utilizing innovative techniques to drive increased customer value and market penetration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the cross-functional team providing vision, motivation, and support and coaching infrastructure to drive the business and achieve portfolio objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Market Access and Country Managers to identify, develop, propose and execute local reimbursement plans, including alignment with appropriate adaptation of European pricing, reimbursement and access strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively lead and build a high performing commercial team by hiring top talent, addressing talent gaps, upskilling and providing career guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take responsibility and accountability to deliver against the agreed commercial and strategic objectives, as well as Quality, Compliance and risk management in the countries of the cluster&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that all business activities are in line with company policies, procedures and local guidelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builds sustainable relationships with local healthcare stakeholders, functions as main partner for local customers and local/ international KOLs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure high quality revenue and volume forecasting and brand investment deployment for the cluster&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develops and implements innovative, multichannel marketing strategies and tactics in the cluster, including the planning and tracking of commercial spent investment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In close collaboration with the Global marketing teams, ensure deep local market and stakeholder insights to inform local tailoring of the strategy and tactics and to help inform the global/regional strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributes to the development of the Global strategic plan and annual tactical plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure detailed pre-launch and post-launch tracking of agreed KPIs to allow early course correction and ensure execution of key tactics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications, Key Skills, and Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Science degree or Business degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive knowledge / experience of working in a bio/pharmaceutical commercial (Sales &amp;amp; Marketing) team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in collaboration in Cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable commercial leadership experience in the biopharmaceutical industry such as a highly successful Sales Manager or Marketing Manager and a strong sales &amp;amp; marketing leader within the specialty therapeutics arena, orphan drugs is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have a track record of successful budget management with an understanding of revenue forecasting and expense budget planning and tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have the ability to build and drive a business, whilst possessing innate ‘market-making’ capabilities with natural self-starter, hands-on, entrepreneurial and innovative attitude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership qualities such as having the ability to attract, motive and retain talent and drive a culture of collaboration, engagement and motivation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to provide strategic input at Global level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding knowledge of the Rare Disease space, including Market Access key success factors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong network/matrix stakeholder communications skills with both regional and in-country teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business and financial acumen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relentless external customer and patient focus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding strategic thinking combined with strong execution leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspirational leader, able to energize and motivate cross-functional teams and Sales Force&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Autonomous working style, pragmatic and operationally oriented, excellent planning and organizing skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sense of urgency, ethics and responsibility&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent command of written and spoken English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Openness to travel approximately is required - 60% domestically and some internationally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Alnylam:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Alnylam Pharmaceuticals (Nasdaq: ALNY) has led the translation of RNA interference (RNAi) into a whole new class of innovative medicines with the potential to transform the lives of people afflicted with rare and more prevalent diseases. Based on Nobel Prize-winning science, RNAi therapeutics represent a powerful, clinically validated approach to treating diseases at their genetic source by “interfering” with mRNA that cause or contribute to disease. Since our founding in 2002, Alnylam has led the RNAi Revolution and continues to turn scientific possibility into reality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our culture:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Our people-first culture is guided by our core values: fiercely innovative, open culture, purposeful urgency, passion for excellence, and commitment to people, and these values influence how we work and the business decisions we make. Thanks to feedback from our employees over the years, we’ve been fortunate to be named a top employer around the world. Alnylam is extremely proud to have been recognized as one of Science Magazine’s Top Biopharma Employers, one of America&#39;s Most Responsible Companies for 2024 by Newsweek, a Fast Company Best Workplace for Innovators, and a Great Place to Work in Canada, France, Italy, Spain, Switzerland, and UK – among others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Alnylam, we commit to an inclusive recruitment process and equal employment opportunity. We are dedicated to building an environment where employees can feel that they belong, can bring their authentic selves to work, and achieve to their full potential. By empowering employees to embrace their unique differences at work, our business grows stronger with advanced and original thinking, allowing us to bring groundbreaking medicines to patients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before applying, please review Alnylam&#39;s ⁠Candidate&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://alnylampolicies.com/&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; regarding how Alnylam handles Personal Data you provide with your application for employment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-CC1&amp;nbsp;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;Find Jobs in Switzerland on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Flexport:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Flexport, we believe global trade can move the human race forward. That’s why it’s our mission to make global commerce so easy there will be more of it. We’re shaping the future of a $10T industry with solutions powered by innovative technology and exceptional people. Today, companies of all sizes—from emerging brands to Fortune 500s—use Flexport technology to move more than $19B of merchandise across 112 countries a year.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The recent global supply chain crisis has put Flexport center stage as we continue to play a pivotal role in how goods move around the world. We are proud to have the support of the best investors in the game who believe in our mission, solutions and people. Ready to tackle global challenges that impact business, society, and the environment? Come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and grow with us! Join Flexport Switzerland as a Founding Account Executive&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;This is the first Account Executive position on the ground in Switzerland, Flexport’s newest market. As part of the founding commercial team, you’ll build the territory from the ground up: shaping the go-to-market approach, establishing our first customer relationships, and defining how Flexport operates and wins in the Swiss market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll drive complex, high-value deals and build long-term strategic partnerships with medium-sized and large customers. These are multi-stakeholder sales cycles that often span regions, business units, decision layers and require the ability to translate solutions into value&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll operate with a high degree of autonomy, shaping deal strategy, influencing executive stakeholders, and orchestrating cross-functional teams to deliver differentiated, value-driven solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Build pipeline and dive deep into the market&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a strategic pipeline through your own prospecting, account planning, and in close collaboration with our SDR team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Flexport at industry events, associations and networks to build the brand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share market insight and customer feedback with leadership, and help shape the Swiss sales playbook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Win new business&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle, from first meeting to signed contract, and meet or exceed quota.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead discovery with senior stakeholders in logistics, procurement, finance, IT, and leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design integrated, multi-product Flexport solutions aligned to customer priorities and backed by clear business cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead pricing, negotiation, and contracting, bringing in Ops, Finance, Legal, and Product as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep forecasts and pipeline accurate in Salesforce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Launch and grow customers&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own onboarding so new customers ramp smoothly and become our Swiss references.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build long-term relationships with senior customer stakeholders and hand accounts over smoothly to Account Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to deal reviews, sales best practices, and peer coaching across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of B2B sales closing complex deals with several decision-makers, with consistent quota attainment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Logistics, freight forwarding or supply chain experience, combined with tech sales acumen: you can sell a platform as confidently as a freight service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep understanding of the Swiss market and local business landscape, with the credibility to engage senior buyers from day one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter who ramps fast, stays curious and does well with ambiguity and no established playbook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence, plus value-based discovery and negotiation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent German and English; French and/or Italian are a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An opportunity to contribute to one of the fastest-growing companies, where you’ll have the chance to create a global impact while being part of a thriving multinational environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity program: every team member becomes a shareholder, aligning our success with yours. As a private company in a multi-trillion-dollar industry, you have a direct stake in our collective growth and success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Program through Aetna Resources for Living: Flexport provides an employer-sponsored program at no cost to you and your household members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental leave benefit: Flexport is here to support you and your family in one of the most important times in life, the birth of a child. Our parental leave program allows both mothers and partners to take time off from work for pregnancy, childbirth, and to bond with your new child.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commitment to Equal Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; At Flexport, our ability to fulfill our mission of making global commerce easy and accessible relies on having a diverse, dedicated and engaged workforce. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, physical and mental disability, health status, marital and family status, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military and veteran status, and any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
