&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;AST SpaceMobile and our global partners are building the first and only space-based cellular broadband network to be accessible by standard smartphones. Called SpaceMobile, this ultra-powerful network is being designed to provide connectivity at 4G/5G speeds everywhere on the planet – on land, at sea and in flight.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Position Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a &lt;strong&gt;SoC/ASIC Architect&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Silicon Team in Edinburgh is a small, highly focused group responsible for developing high‑value silicon that is core to AST’s mission of &lt;em&gt;“Connecting the unconnected” - &lt;/em&gt;delivering the world’s first space‑based mobile broadband network.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team works collaboratively to define and build next‑generation silicon, exploring advanced silicon technologies to continuously improve performance, capability, and efficiency. This is a hands‑on environment where silicon decisions directly impact AST’s ability to deliver a global communications network from space.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will drive the architectural definition of complex System‑on‑Chips (SoCs) critical to AST’s satellite communications platforms. You will translate system and product requirements into high‑quality architectural specifications, guiding technical decisions from concept through implementation. Working closely with cross‑functional internal teams and external partners, you will help ensure timely delivery of robust, high‑performance silicon solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;•&amp;nbsp;Work cross‑functionally with hardware, software, verification, product, and systems teams to define and deliver SoC architectures.&lt;br&gt;• Own and author high‑quality architecture and specification documentation.&lt;br&gt;• Guide design trade‑offs across performance, power, area, security, and schedule.&lt;br&gt;• Engage in design, verification, and implementation reviews to ensure architectural integrity.&lt;br&gt;• Support silicon bring‑up and debug through close collaboration with validation and software teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BEng in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or a related field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Demonstrated capability delivering high‑quality architectural specifications.&lt;br&gt;• Strong background in hardware and digital design.&lt;br&gt;• Experience working on complex SoCs or ASICs from inception to tapeout.&lt;br&gt;• Background in some or all of the following areas: Silicon security, Boot flow, CPU architecture, Memory subsystems, Interconnects / NoC, High‑speed interfaces, Peripheral subsystems.&lt;br&gt;• Competency in Python scripting or programming.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;•&amp;nbsp;Master’s or PhD degree in a relevant technical discipline.&lt;br&gt;• Solid understanding of digital signal processing.&lt;br&gt;• Experience with MATLAB is a plus.&lt;br&gt;• Prior experience working on RF, communications or signal‑processing ASICs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Soft Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Ability to work collaboratively across hardware, software, verification, product, systems, validation, and software teams.&lt;br&gt;• Ability to work closely with internal teams and external partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technology Stack:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Python scripting or programming&lt;br&gt;• MATLAB&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Ability to work in a standard office environment and use a computer for extended periods.&lt;br&gt;• Occasional travel may be required to visit suppliers or other AST SpaceMobile design centers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This job description may not be inclusive to the duties and responsibilities listed. Additional tasks may be assigned to the employee from time to time or the scope of the job may change as needed by business demands&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;AST SpaceMobile is an Equal Opportunity, at will Employer; employment is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

Established in 2004, OLIVER is the world's first and only specialist in designing, building, and running bespoke in-house agencies and marketing ecosystems for brands. We partner with over 300 clients in 40+ countries and counting. Our unique model drives creativity and efficiency, allowing us to deliver tailored solutions that resonate deeply with audiences.&nbsp;
As a part of The Brandtech Group, we're at the forefront of leveraging cutting-edge AI technology to revolutionise how we create and deliver work. Our AI solutions enhance efficiency, spark creativity, and drive insightful decision-making, empowering our teams to produce innovative and impactful results.&nbsp;E-commerce Data Analyst
Location: Weybridge, Surrey, United Kingdom
&nbsp;
Established in 2004, Inside Ideas Group is a rapidly growing global agency network that helps clients drive their businesses forward from the inside. We partner with over 300 clients in more than 40 countries, delivering ideas, technology and creativity that make a measurable impact.&nbsp;
As part of The&nbsp;Brandtech&nbsp;Group, we are pioneers in using advanced AI technologies to transform the way we create,&nbsp;optimise&nbsp;and deliver work. Our AI capabilities enhance efficiency, support smart decision making and unlock new levels of creativity for our teams and clients.&nbsp;
We are now looking for a skilled Data Analyst to join our onsite team supporting in London.&nbsp;
About the Role&nbsp;
As the E-commerce Data Analyst, you will be responsible for delivering insight that drives improvements across the full commercial ecosystem spanning customer experience on, retailer investment effectiveness, marketing and sales performance, and the broader post-purchase, onboarding and promotional landscape.&nbsp;
A core part of your remit will be the design, build and ongoing management of a marketing and sales performance dashboard, underpinned by Google BigQuery and delivered in Looker Studio. This will serve as a critical decision-making tool for marketing, e-commerce, retail and CX teams surfacing insight such as campaign uplift, halo effects, retailer investment impact and share performance across products and markets.&nbsp;
Alongside this, you will analyse customer journeys, benchmark competitors, oversee content performance and support the planning and execution of onboarding and e-commerce promotions using platforms like GWI to create digital personas and audience profiles.&nbsp;
You will collaborate closely with CX, marketing, product and e-commerce teams as well as HQ and local market stakeholders to ensure insight informs decisions at every stage.&nbsp;
This role requires strong analytical capability,&nbsp;expertise&nbsp;in data modelling and SQL, and the ability to translate complex commercial questions into dashboard logic and actionable recommendations.&nbsp;
What You Will Be Doing&nbsp;
Marketing &amp; Sales Performance Analytics&nbsp;&nbsp;

Design, build and&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;a marketing and sales performance dashboard in Looker Studio, underpinned by&nbsp;BigQuery, combining sell-out sales data, market volume and share data, and campaign activity logs.&nbsp;


Define the underlying data model, transform source&nbsp;files&nbsp;and design the reporting layer to support consistent, scalable KPI delivery.&nbsp;


Identify&nbsp;and quantify the impact of retailer investment, including uplift in sales and market share during campaign periods.&nbsp;


Analyse correlations between campaign activity and commercial performance to&nbsp;determine&nbsp;which marketing levers are most effective.&nbsp;


Measure and report on halo effects across products and retailers resulting from promotional and campaign activity.&nbsp;


Define and calculate key performance metrics including uplift, baseline, market share, activity&nbsp;intensity&nbsp;and halo effects.&nbsp;


Work with GFK&nbsp;or other syndicated market data sources to enrich performance analysis with market volume and share context.&nbsp;

Customer Experience &amp; Digital Analytics&nbsp;

Conduct analysis of the current customer experience, including user behaviour, content and campaign performance and conversion pathways.&nbsp;


Benchmark key customer journeys against competitor websites to&nbsp;identify&nbsp;gaps and opportunities.&nbsp;


Provide&nbsp;regular insight into paid promotions, post-purchase&nbsp;experience&nbsp;and customer satisfaction trends.&nbsp;


Support planning, optimisation and operational management of post-purchase and onboarding experience.&nbsp;


Analyse content utilisation, engagement and drop-off points, and recommend enhancements.&nbsp;


Collaborate with HQ and local teams on onboarding content production and implementation.&nbsp;


Support feature management including evaluation, testing&nbsp;performance&nbsp;and monitoring adoption, with ongoing analysis of content effectiveness and customer experience updates.&nbsp;


Reporting, Dashboards &amp; Stakeholder Insight&nbsp;


Build and&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;dashboards, reports and ad hoc analyses across customer experience, onboarding, e-commerce, retail&nbsp;performance&nbsp;and promotion activity.&nbsp;


Translate data into clear insights that guide decision-making within marketing, CX, digital and commercial teams.&nbsp;


Present findings clearly to stakeholders at all levels, ensuring insight is embedded in planning and operational processes.&nbsp;


Use platforms like GWI to build digital personas and audience profiles that support broader marketing planning.&nbsp;

What You Need to Be Great in This Role&nbsp;
Essential&nbsp;

Proven experience as a data or insight analyst within digital, e-commerce, retail,&nbsp;marketing&nbsp;or agency environments.&nbsp;


Strong&nbsp;proficiency&nbsp;in Google&nbsp;BigQuery and advanced SQL, including data modelling and reporting layer design.&nbsp;


Hands-on experience building dashboards in Looker Studio, with a clear understanding of how to structure underlying data models for robust, scalable dashboard performance.&nbsp;


Demonstrable experience combining sell-out sales, market&nbsp;share&nbsp;and campaign activity datasets to generate commercial insight.&nbsp;


Ability to define and calculate metrics including uplift, baseline, market share, activity&nbsp;intensity&nbsp;and halo effects.&nbsp;


Strong marketing analytics capability, including campaign effectiveness measurement across paid and promotional channels.&nbsp;


Good understanding of digital customer journeys, content performance&nbsp;metrics&nbsp;and e-commerce KPIs.&nbsp;


Experience with analytics platforms such as Google Analytics GA4, Adobe Analytics or similar.&nbsp;


Excellent communication and storytelling ability — capable of translating complex business questions into dashboard logic and presenting findings clearly to non-technical audiences.&nbsp;


Experience working with multi-market teams and managing stakeholder expectations across business functions.&nbsp;


A passion for data-driven decision-making and an interest in how AI can enhance analytics workflows.&nbsp;

Preferred:&nbsp;

Proficiency&nbsp;in Python (pandas) for data transformation,&nbsp;automation&nbsp;and workflow scripting.&nbsp;


Broader experience with Google Cloud Platform (GCP), including automating data ingestion and transformation workflows.&nbsp;


Experience working in retail,&nbsp;e-commerce&nbsp;or retailer media environments.&nbsp;


Familiarity with GfK or other syndicated market data sources.&nbsp;


Experience with&nbsp;additional&nbsp;BI tools such as Tableau or Power BI.&nbsp;

Our Values&nbsp;
Be Ambitious to succeed Be Imaginative to push the boundaries of&nbsp;what's&nbsp;possible Be Inspirational to do groundbreaking work Be always learning and listening to understand Be Results-focused to exceed expectations Be actively pro-inclusive and anti-racist across our community,&nbsp;clients&nbsp;and creations&nbsp;
