&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The AI Teams at Agile Robots&lt;/strong&gt; are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Computer Vision Engineer (m/f/d) Robotic Manipulation&lt;/strong&gt;, who will build vision and software components that let our robots recognize and handle objects in close-to-industry applications. The stack combines in-house software with external research models, so you will help bring new results onto real robots without breaking what already runs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vision Components:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and integrate learning-based vision components, such as object detection, segmentation, and pose estimation, that give robots the input they need to grasp and manipulate objects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Software Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and implement software components, architectures, and applications for AI-enhanced robotic systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Robot Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Bring applications onto a changing range of robots and sensors, including dual-arm and humanoid platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Research Transfer:&lt;/strong&gt; Follow current research in computer vision and robot learning, and evaluate which external models and components are ready to integrate into the stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stack Maintenance:&lt;/strong&gt; Review, test, and maintain the shared software stack so that existing applications keep running as new components are added.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Background:&lt;/strong&gt; Degree in robotics, computer vision, computer science, electrical or mechanical engineering, or a related field, or equivalent experience, with around four years of professional experience building robotics or vision software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Computer Vision:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience training, adapting, and deploying current learning-based vision models, including pretrained vision and vision-language models, on real camera data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ROS 2:&lt;/strong&gt; Professional experience developing robotics software with ROS 2.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programming:&lt;/strong&gt; Production experience in C++ and Python, working with CMake, Git, and shell scripting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beneficial Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vision-Based Manipulation:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience using camera input to guide grasping or manipulation, for example grasp pose estimation or visual servoing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Humanoid Platforms:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience developing software for dual-arm or humanoid robots.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Motion Control:&lt;/strong&gt; Working knowledge of robot motion planning and control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Task Logic:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience structuring robot task logic with state machines or behavior trees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;TranslationField-module__fieldItemName___Q0F_7 TranslationField-module__aboutUsWrapper___WXJpq&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
