&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot; lang=&quot;EN-CA&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot;&gt;Please read our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.wppmedia.com/pages/privacy-policy#:~:text=WPP%20Media%20Privacy%20Notice%20for%20Recruitment&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot; lang=&quot;EN-CA&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot;&gt;for more information on how we process the information you provide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:276}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About WPP Media&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. With exceptional talent, trusted data and intelligence, and world-class partnerships – all united by our pioneering agentic marketing platform, WPP Open – we help clients navigate change, capture opportunity, and deliver transformational growth. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP Media is WPP&#39;s AI-driven media operating unit, bringing together media, data, and partnerships to deliver creative personalisation at scale. Connected through WPP Open and powered by Open Intelligence, clients see exactly where, how, and why their media investment is working.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;wppmedia.com&quot;&gt;wppmedia.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2931 - Associate Director, Activation &amp;amp; Delivery, GCS&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary and Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Search &amp;amp; Ecommerce Account Director to lead the strategic development, execution, and performance of integrated biddable activity across &lt;strong&gt;Google Ads (Search, Shopping, Performance Max)&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Amazon Search&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a senior leader within the team, you will be responsible for &lt;strong&gt;defining and delivering best-in-class search and ecommerce strategies&lt;/strong&gt;, ensuring alignment with broader client business goals and full-funnel media objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will act as the &lt;strong&gt;senior client contact&lt;/strong&gt;, working with stakeholders at Director level and above, while leading cross-functional teams and offshore delivery hubs to execute against strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role combines &lt;strong&gt;deep platform expertise, strategic leadership, and operational oversight&lt;/strong&gt;, ensuring campaigns are executed to the highest standard while continuously driving innovation and growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the development of holistic Search &amp;amp; Ecommerce strategies across:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Google Ads (Search, Shopping, Performance Max)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Amazon Search (Sponsored Ads ecosystem)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure strategies are aligned to client business objectives, KPIs, and commercial priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate broader marketing strategy into channel-specific activation frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify growth opportunities across demand capture (Search) and retail media (Amazon)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive integration between Search, Ecommerce, and wider media channels (Paid Social, Programmatic, SEO)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop forward-thinking POVs on industry trends, platform developments, and emerging opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client and Stakeholder Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary senior contact for Search &amp;amp; Ecommerce across your client portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships with senior stakeholders, becoming a trusted strategic advisor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead client meetings, presentations, quarterly reviews, and strategic planning sessions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clearly articulate performance, insights, and forward strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to grow client investment and expand scope&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Performance and Campaign&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain ultimate accountability for performance delivery across all Search &amp;amp; Ecommerce activity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee campaign execution across Google Ads and Amazon platforms, ensuring alignment with strategy
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure robust optimisation frameworks are in place across:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bidding &amp;amp; automation (e.g., Smart Bidding, PMAX optimisation)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed optimisation (Shopping / Amazon)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Query, audience, and keyword strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead performance reviews, identifying risks and opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure rigorous testing frameworks are defined and executed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all campaigns are delivered &lt;strong&gt;on time, within budget, and to the highest standards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain strong governance across:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;QA processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financial management and invoicing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Platform best practice adherence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive improvements in workflows, automation, and efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure clear documentation of processes and ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead development of &lt;strong&gt;test &amp;amp; learn roadmaps&lt;/strong&gt; across Search and Ecommerce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to leverage new platform capabilities (e.g., PMAX, AI bidding, Amazon innovations)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to agency thought leadership, case studies, and award submissions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively participate in the wider Search and Commerce communities within WPP Media&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Onshore–Offshore Delivery Model&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and manage ways of working between onshore strategy teams and offshore execution teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure offshore teams are set up for success with:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear briefs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Defined processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;QA frameworks and performance standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee output quality across offshore Account Managers and Executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive scalability, efficiency, and operational excellence across delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a team of Account Managers and Account Executives (onshore and offshore)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide coaching, mentorship, and performance management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure effective workload allocation, prioritisation, and delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support hiring and team growth aligned to client needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a high-performing, collaborative, and innovative team culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience across:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Google Ads (Search, Shopping, Performance Max)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Amazon Search / Retail Media ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of leading performance-driven search and ecommerce strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of full-funnel media strategy and cross-channel integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced analytical skills with ability to translate data into actionable insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing large-scale, complex accounts and budgets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong client leadership experience, including senior stakeholder management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing and developing multi-layered teams (including offshore models)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of bidding strategies, feed-based media, automation, and measurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Life at WPP Media &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our passion for shaping the next era of media includes investing in our employees to help them do their best work, and we&#39;re just as committed to employee growth as we are to responsible media investment. WPP Media employees can tap into the global WPP Media &amp;amp; WPP networks to pursue their passions, grow their networks, and learn at the cutting edge of marketing and advertising. We have a variety of employee resource groups and host frequent in-office events showcasing team wins, sharing thought leadership, and celebrating holidays and milestone events. Our benefits include competitive medical, group retirement plans, vision, and dental insurance, significant paid time off, preferential partner discounts, and employee mental health awareness days.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP Media is an equal opportunity employer and considers applicants for all positions without discrimination or regard to particular characteristics. We are committed to fostering a culture of respect in which everyone feels they belong and has the same opportunities to progress in their careers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe the best work happens when we&#39;re together, fostering creativity, collaboration, and connection. That&#39;s why we&#39;ve adopted a hybrid approach, with teams in the office around four days a week. If you require accommodations or flexibility, please discuss this with the hiring team during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note this is a UK based role and requires individuals to have the right to work in this location&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please read our Privacy Notice (https://www.wppmedia.com/pages/privacy-policy) for more information on how we process the information you provide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Promoted&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot; lang=&quot;EN-CA&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot;&gt;Please read our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.wppmedia.com/pages/privacy-policy#:~:text=WPP%20Media%20Privacy%20Notice%20for%20Recruitment&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot; lang=&quot;EN-CA&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot;&gt;for more information on how we process the information you provide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:276}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Forward Deployed AI Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;DEPT® is a Growth Invention company built to help the world’s most ambitious brands grow faster. Operating at the intersection of technology and marketing, our 4,000+ specialists deliver growth invention services across Brand &amp;amp; Media, Experience, Commerce, CRM, and Technology &amp;amp; Data. We’re 50|50 tech and marketing, partner-led, and first to move. Clients include Google, Lufthansa, Meta, eBay, and OpenAI. We have been certified B Corp and Climate Neutral since 2021.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Global AI Strategy &amp;amp; Solutions defines how DEPT®’s clients respond as AI agents become the primary layer between customers and brands. The Future of the Customer Journey (FCJ) is the team’s flagship offer: it maps how AI systems intermediate customer journeys, diagnoses where a brand’s product reality diverges from what AI systems say about it, and directs investment accordingly. Growth and strategy teams across markets are selling and delivering it now.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a&amp;nbsp;Forward Deployed AI Engineer, you are an embedded builder inside that motion. You will sit with growth and strategy teams, understand the problem in front of them, and answer with working software rather than documentation. You will convert FCJ methodology into agentic components, prototypes, and internal tools, and integrate with infrastructure that lets new prototypes appear in days. When needed, you will work across global client projects on a partially billable basis, making sure the firm-wide strategy is captured and implemented properly rather than reinvented market by market. As components mature, you will collaborate with product and craft teams to keep everything compatible with the long-term platform and hand over cleanly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be given broad problem statements to help collaborate and solve, not specific product ideas and features to create. We are not looking for someone to lead on devops or CI/CD, this is about having great ideas that are sensitive to our clients’ real challenges, and shipping prototypes and strategic tools rapidly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your most important collaboration is with the FCJ core team on the global growth strategy: deciding what gets built next, for which market, to unlock which engagement. The toolchain will keep changing underneath you, new models, new vendor products, new technology-partner platforms, and that is the point. This role suits an engineer who learns by shipping and treats every new AI product as something to master in the field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the FCJ core team on the global growth strategy, converting methodology into working agentic components, prototypes, and internal tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with growth and strategy teams to understand their problems and provide working solutions at prototype pace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across global client projects on a partially billable basis, ensuring the firm-wide FCJ strategy is captured and implemented consistently across markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product and craft teams where necessary to document integration paths, maintain platform compatibility, and hand over validated components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with technology partners to evaluate, adopt, and integrate new AI products; maintain an AI-native toolchain and share what works across markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience prototyping and shipping software in any modern backend language (Python, TypeScript, Go, or similar), with the ability to leverage AI tooling to spin up prototype frontends and APIs quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building applications across the mainstream LLM model families (Gemini, GPT, Claude), connecting models to enterprise data and tools using patterns such as retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) and skills-based agent systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in working with APIs to connect different services, authentication, data exchange, and integration across platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing agentic systems with orchestration frameworks such as LangChain, LangGraph, or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-native way of working: AI tooling is the default across coding, research, and delivery, with comfort spanning the tools in use across different markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a forward-deployed, customer engineering, solutions engineering, or applied AI role within an agency, consultancy, or AI company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting working software to non-technical stakeholders, including strategists and clients, and iterating live on their feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of emerging integration standards such as OpenAPI and Model Context Protocol (MCP) for connecting agents to business systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of any of the following: paid media, social platforms, user behaviour, agentic commerce, or generative engine optimisation (GEO).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with evaluation, tracing, and observability for LLM applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated learning mindset: a record of adopting new AI products from technology partners quickly, learning by doing rather than waiting for training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A flexible, hybrid working policy (2 days from the office in London).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An excellent salary based on experience and equal pay policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension, free private healthcare, mental health support, and company sick pay scheme.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;26 days paid holiday (plus UK Bank Holidays).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help getting you to work with a season ticket loan and cycle to work scheme.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced family friendly policies to support new parents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social and Cultural Events, plenty of opportunities to connect with colleagues through organised activities and celebrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspirational Talks, bringing the outside in with regular guest speakers and events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and Development, supporting your growth with continuous opportunities to learn and advance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Buddy Programme: You will be paired with a ‘Buddy’ to help you through your first weeks’ at DEPT®.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A reputation for doing good. DEPT® has been a Certified &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.deptagency.com/en-gb/insight/dept-is-a-certified-b-corporation/&quot;&gt;B Corp® since 2021&lt;/a&gt; and named ‘Agency of the Year’ at both The Lovies and The Webby Awards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Awesome clients. Whether big or small, local or global — at DEPT® you’ll get the opportunity to work with clients of all sizes and across all industries. And we celebrate all of our successes together!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity for possibility. We want to enable you to do what you do best and help you develop your skills further with training, development and certifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global annual &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.deptagency.com/dept-cares-day-2023/&quot;&gt;DEPT® Cares Month&lt;/a&gt; in which employees come together and donate their skills to support local charities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why DEPT®?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a Growth Invention company built to help the world’s most ambitious brands grow faster. Operating at the intersection of technology and marketing, we create what is next by pioneering ideas, acting fast, and moving further because standing still just is not in our DNA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are drawn to people who stay curious, move with intent, and never stop inventing. Our culture runs on three values: better together, relentlessly curious, and get sh*t done. It is how we work, how we grow, and how we make things that matter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DEPT®, you will find the freedom to explore, the space to collaborate, and the trust to make a real impact for our clients, for each other, and for the world we are helping to build..&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity &amp;amp; Inclusion&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DEPT®, we take pride in creating an inclusive workplace where everyone has an equal opportunity to thrive. We actively seek to recruit, develop, nurture, and retain talented individuals from diverse backgrounds, with varying skills and perspectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Not sure you meet all qualifications? Apply, and let us decide! Research shows that women and members of underrepresented groups tend not to apply for jobs when they think they may not meet every requirement, when in fact they do. We believe in giving everyone a fair chance to shine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We also encourage you to reach out to us and discuss any reasonable adjustments we can make to support you throughout the recruitment process and your time with us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Want to know more about our dedication to diversity, equity, and inclusion? Check out our efforts&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.deptagency.com/the-good-company/&quot;&gt; here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

Ajax Systems is an international tech company and the largest manufacturer of security systems in Europe, with over 4.5 million end users and 330K PRO users in more than 180 countries worldwide. The company offers end-to-end solutions for protecting homes and businesses оf any scale. To date, Ajax product portfolio includes 280 devices for intrusion protection, video surveillance, fire and life safety, and comfort and automation.&nbsp; The company employs 5, 000 specialists.&nbsp;
We develop local teams because we understand local experts best comprehend market specifics. The company has sales representatives worldwide, including Italy, Spain, Germany, France, the United Kingdom, the USA, Australia, South Africa and other regions. The Global Business Development team is like-minded people who share the ambitious goals of Ajax Systems.&nbsp;
The best software combined with powerful hardware has forever changed the perception of security systems for users and industry professionals. Being recognized at the biggest specialized exhibitions such as IFSEC, Expoprotection and Intersec, as well as winning prestigious awards from industry-leading media like PSI magazine and GIT SECURITY, today Ajax is one of the most awarded security systems in Europe.
Ajax Systems production includes four factories, two of which are located in Ukraine, one in Turkey and one in Vietnam. At the same time, the company's certification according to the ISO 14001 standard ensures a minimal impact of production on the environment. The selection of components for Ajax device manufacturing is determined by the presence of manufacturer declarations confirming compliance with RoHS requirements.
The company emerged against the backdrop of revolution and war. That's why resilience is the cornerstone of the brand's DNA, and the fight against evil by creating the best security and automation devices is Ajax unwavering mission.Responsibilities:
Assist technically business development manager for customer meetings;
Conduct technical seminars, exhibitions, presentations, webinars on the product (for customers and company employees);
Present new&nbsp; products and new features for Ajax Systems distributors, as well as installers;
Teach technical staff at distributors and dealers to increase their knowledge of products and technology;
Promote and introduce product solutions according to customer thesis, technical consultation, and support of key clients;
Market research and сomparative сharacteristics of products of the competitors;
Develop long-term relationships with key partners of the company;
​​Beta test product features and write technical documentation for new products or solutions, and collaborate with the rest of the team;
Analyze customer needs in collaboration with the sales department.
Key requirements:
University Degree in IT /electronic engineering.
Professional experience with Alarm Systems, video surveillance, security, telecommunications and other related areas.&nbsp;
An excellent working knowledge of Alarm systems, IP CCTV.
Experience in installing/designing alarm, video surveillance systems, fire alarms, access control or other security systems.
Experience of training delivery or public speaking (as an advantage).
Strong communication skills.
Available to travel across the region.
Has an outgoing personality, enthusiastic and can work independently.
We offer:
An opportunity to work in one of the most recognized and innovative security manufacturers.
An opportunity to take on new challenges, advance your career, and make a meaningful impact.
Opportunity to be part of a fast-paced and dynamic environment that encourages creativity, critical thinking, and the exploration of new ideas.&nbsp;
Competitive compensation that includes a base salary and performance-related bonuses.
Car allowance and all business expenses covered by the company.
