&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ihre Mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie begleiten Enterprise-Kunden dabei, den Mehrwert unserer Agentic-Commerce-Architektur – einschließlich Composable Commerce, Frontend und Connect – zu maximieren und flexible, zukunftssichere Tech-Stacks aufzubauen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie übersetzen neue Produktfeatures und -funktionen in klare Geschäftsergebnisse und stimmen diese direkt auf die strategischen Ziele und zentralen ROI-Kennzahlen des jeweiligen Kunden ab.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie treiben Kundenbeziehungen proaktiv voran und leiten wirkungsvolle Strategic Business Reviews (SBRs), um die Kundenbindung zu stärken, die Plattformnutzung zu steigern und langfristiges Wachstum zu beschleunigen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie arbeiten eng mit dem Produktmanagement zusammen, vertreten die Bedürfnisse unserer Kunden und liefern entscheidendes Feedback, das die Roadmap unserer neuesten Produktinnovationen mitgestaltet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie arbeiten nahtlos und teamübergreifend mit Sales, Product und Support zusammen, bringen tiefgehendes technisches und kaufmännisches Know-how ein und sichern so langfristig den Erfolg unserer Enterprise-Kunden.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie repräsentieren commercetools in Webinaren, Kundenfallstudien und Beratungsgremien, um Kundenerfolge sichtbar zu machen und das Engagement innerhalb der Community zu fördern.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie übernehmen eine zentrale Rolle bei der Weiterentwicklung globaler Customer-Success-Frameworks, treiben interne Prozessverbesserungen voran und gestalten die langfristige operative Strategie der Abteilung mit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie agieren intern und extern als anerkannte:r Fachexpert:in, unterstützen Teammitglieder als Mentor:in, fördern die funktionsübergreifende Zusammenarbeit und tragen dazu bei, die gemeinsamen Standards unserer Customer-Success-Praxis weiter anzuheben.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie fungieren als Eskalationsinstanz und arbeiten mit dem Product-Support-Team zusammen, um Probleme schnell zu lösen. Auch in anspruchsvollen Eskalationssituationen bleiben Sie ruhig, professionell und besonnen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Was Sie mitbringen – Ihr Profil&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mindestens fünf Jahre Erfahrung in einem High-Touch-Tech-Umfeld mit nachweisbaren Erfolgen im Bereich Customer Success, Pre-Sales oder Technical Consulting – idealerweise in den Branchen E-Commerce oder Retail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deutschkenntnisse auf muttersprachlichem Niveau sowie verhandlungssichere Englischkenntnisse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ein tiefes technisches Verständnis moderner API-first- und Headless-Technologien, gepaart mit betriebswirtschaftlichem Denken und der Fähigkeit, komplexe Technologien in messbaren ROI zu übersetzen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Die Fähigkeit, als überzeugende:r und vertrauenswürdige:r Berater:in aufzutreten, Gespräche auf C-Level-Ebene zu führen, Kundenstrategien mitzugestalten und Expansionspotenziale sicher zu identifizieren und zu erschließen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eine strukturierte und agile Arbeitsweise sowie die Fähigkeit, komplexe Accounts über globale, funktionsübergreifende Teams hinweg eigenverantwortlich zu betreuen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eine teamorientierte Persönlichkeit, die in einer dynamischen, internationalen Tech-Kultur aufblüht, sowie eine Reisebereitschaft von bis zu 50 %, um wertvolle Kundenbeziehungen aufzubauen und zu pflegen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Von Vorteil:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Weitere Sprachkenntnisse (Französisch oder Spanisch)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Because work and life are connected, our benefits are too. We’ve designed them to give you the security, flexibility, and opportunities you need to focus on what matters most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🩺 &lt;strong&gt;Comprehensive health benefits&lt;/strong&gt; for you and your dependents, including access to OpenUp for personalized mental health support&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📚 &lt;strong&gt;Learning and development &lt;/strong&gt;opportunities including an annual learning budget, access to self-paced learning platforms and language training, personalized coaching, mentorship, and leadership programs&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🍼 &lt;strong&gt;Family Leave Plus&lt;/strong&gt; gives you additional fully paid weeks of parental leave on top of government-provided leave, so you can spend more time with your new addition&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📈 &lt;strong&gt;Our equity participation program&lt;/strong&gt; allows you to share in our success&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information on our benefits, &lt;a href=&quot;https://commercetools.com/careers/our-benefits&quot;&gt;visit this page.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come as you are. Build with us.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your unique perspective is essential to our success. We are committed to building a team that reflects the world around us because we know it’s the only way to build the future. We celebrate our differences and have created a hiring process that’s fair, inclusive, and designed to let your talent shine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We proudly welcome applicants of every race, color, religion, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, and any other part of your identity that makes you who you are. As an equal opportunity employer, we believe that our strength lies in our diversity, and we invite you to be a part of our global community.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information on our diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging practices, &lt;a href=&quot;https://commercetools.com/careers/dei-esg&quot;&gt;visit this page&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div data-ogsc=&quot;black&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ogsc=&quot;&quot; data-ogsb=&quot;yellow&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-ogsc=&quot;&quot; data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;About Acadia Pharmaceuticals&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div data-ogsc=&quot;black&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div data-ogsc=&quot;black&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ogsc=&quot;&quot; data-ogsb=&quot;yellow&quot;&gt;Acadia is committed to turning scientific promise into meaningful innovation that makes the difference for underserved neurological and rare disease communities around the world. Our commercial portfolio includes the first and only FDA-approved treatments for Parkinson’s disease psychosis and Rett syndrome. We are developing the next wave of therapeutic advancements with a robust and diverse pipeline that includes mid- to late-stage programs in Alzheimer’s disease psychosis and Lewy body dementia psychosis, along with earlier-stage programs that address other underserved patient needs. At Acadia, we’re here to be their difference.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Position Summary&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Sr. Medical Director, Germany will lead the development and execution of the local medical affairs strategy together with the field Medical Science Liaisons (MSLs) and in line with the European Medical Affairs strategy and the local country strategy for RETT syndrome including the integrated medical plans with full medical budget ownership and responsibility. Responsibilities will include building and maintaining external stakeholder relationships and collaborations, as well as continuing to position Acadia as a thought leader and valued partner with patient advocacy groups (PAG) and medical/scientific RETT community in Germany. This individual will be responsible for the effectiveness and compliance of scientific exchange conducted to meet the needs of clinicians, patient advocates, and other key external and internal stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Primary Responsibilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide scientific and medical leadership, including development of strategic country medical affairs (post-launch) plans, identifying specific unmet medical needs, and data gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading the local medical affairs team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure strong medical/scientific leadership in coordination and participation in country MRC/MLR procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish appropriate strategic partnerships with Centers of Excellence, KOLs, and PAGs, in areas of scientific interest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure aligned and close cross-functional collaboration, with country GM, Market Access, other relevant country and international staff to optimally manage relationships and ensure alignment and effective execution of the German medical strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and ensure operational medical excellence, in collaboration with EU medical teams and aligned with country strategy, to capture and track key medical tactics and medical (post-launch) activities in Germany.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide medical expertise and editorial support in data dissemination at conferences and in medical journals, as appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Involvement with key HCPs in the exchange of scientific and medical information including Advisory Boards and presentations at national meetings and conferences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain, together with MSLs, close professional relationships with KOLs and emerging scientific leaders in the community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee gathering and reporting field medical insights through existing Veeva CRM system and in line with company rules and requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee and communicate to cross-functional stakeholders the insights the MSL team gains about competitive landscape, unmet needs of physicians and advocacy groups. Develops potential actionable plans to address these local insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manages publication activities, including review and approval of abstracts and manuscripts, local publication strategy and real-world evidence development and compliant collaboration with authors, as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Education/Experience/Skills&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MD highly preferred; PhD, PharmD, or an equivalent qualification may also be considered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of Medical Affairs leadership experience in the biopharmaceutical industry in Germany or the DACH region; broader regional experience is advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior team-management experience is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Substantial rare-disease—preferably neurological—experience in Germany and/or the DACH region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive knowledge of the German healthcare system and applicable national rules and regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience coordinating and participating in national MLR/MRC procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging with rare-disease patient advocacy groups is highly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Skills&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive knowledge to critically appraise studies and clinical evidence to allow engagement on higher scientific level with HCPs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In depth understanding of compliance and regulatory requirements, including extensive personal experience and expertise with MRC/MLR procedures, for pharmaceutical Medical Affairs, R&amp;amp;D and Commercial activities in Germany.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, collaboration, and presentation skills, and experience in the delivery of scientific presentations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agile, independent and proactive working style.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal sense of purpose, confidence, and stand fest in challenging situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build strong cross-functional and cross-company relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate and share information to contribute to the planning process and execute the agreed local Medical (pre)launch plan, together with MSL team, and in line with Regional Medical Affairs strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in German at native or near-native level and strong English proficiency are required, with the ability to communicate complex details clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel both locally and internationally is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#NC1 #LI-HYBRID&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;What we offer US-based Employees:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive base, bonus, new hire and ongoing equity packages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental, and vision insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer-paid life, disability, business travel and EAP coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) Plan with a fully vested company match 1:1 up to 5%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Stock Purchase Plan with a 2-year purchase price lock-in&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ vacation days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;13 -15 paid holidays, including office closure between December 24th and January 1st&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10 days of paid sick time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid parental leave benefit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition assistance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement (US-based Employees): &lt;/strong&gt;Studies have shown that women and people of color are less likely to apply for jobs unless they believe they meet every one of the qualifications in the exact way they are described in job postings. We are committed to building a diverse, equitable, inclusive, and innovative company, and we are looking for the BEST candidate for the job. That candidate may be one who comes from a less traditional background or may meet the qualifications in a different way. We strongly encourage you to apply, especially if the reason you are the best candidate isn’t exactly what we describe here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is the policy of Acadia to provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and employment applicants without regard to considerations of race, including related to hairstyle, color, religion or religious creed, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, gender transition, country of origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, physical or mental disability, genetic information, legally-protected medical condition or information, marital status, domestic partner status, family care status, military caregiver status, veteran or military status (including reserve status, National Guard status, and military service or obligation), status as a victim of domestic violence, sexual assault or stalking, enrollment in a public assistance program, or any basis protected under federal, state or local law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an equal opportunity employer, Acadia is committed to a diverse workforce. If you are a qualified individual with a disability or a disabled veteran, you have the right to request a reasonable accommodation. Furthermore, you may request additional support if you are unable or limited in your ability to use or access Acadia’s career website due to your disability, along with any accommodations throughout the interview process. To request or inquire about your reasonable accommodation, please complete our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/43db301ada19415fa7ab365633993f33&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Reasonable Accommodation Request Form&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;or contact us at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a ----- -----
&lt;p&gt;Please note that reasonable accommodations granted throughout the recruiting process are not guaranteed to be the same accommodations given if hired. A new request will need to be submitted for any ADA accommodations after starting employment.&lt;/p&gt;
